From d5c2d808bb98b2dd6bf947dbb1546b5e46c625a2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 08:44:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Show the new outcome on the slip and bring the last roll
 back after a reload

The store handles roll_outcome: the roller's slip (a kept gilded die's
too) and the Lightkeeper's felt show the outcome Flourish or Bending
Spoons gave the roll, and the post-roll prompts are worked out again
(#19). A roll_result marked replayed brings the last roll back to the
tray after a reload with Burn and reroll while the server holds it open,
its kept die, the abilities already used and its settled state, with no
dice sound or tumble and no roll bar pop-up; a desk that already shows
that roll only takes what changed, a rolling desk ignores it, and a
replay of the roll the desk is waiting for is its answer (#40). The
roll_settled handler goes, as the server no longer sends it. The felt
and the die skews are keyed on the dice, so a new outcome does not throw
them again. FAQ.md, QUIRKS.md (Fix round 6, rolls) and WEBSOCKET.md
describe it.

Checked: vite build; Chromium at 390x844, 820x1180 and 1366x768 on the
player's and the Lightkeeper's desks (Flourish on a plain and a kept
gilded roll, reload, Burn after reload, a reload while another roll
settles it, a dropped socket, a server restart).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WaLz6UBTQ5XaTKSYwqeMKA
